      "writtenOn": "2015-01-02T18:00:59Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "My initial implementation relies on the fact that irq \u0026 hi are always serialized and that the attention packet is only sent when an HPD change has occurred.  So while spec refers to two states I see them as single 2bit state field (0\u003d\u003dlow, 1\u003d\u003dhi, 2\u003d\u003dirq, 3\u003d\u003dundef).\n\nIf that is flawed then you\u0027re correct.  If not then irq\u003d\u003d1 lvl\u003d\u003d1 should never happen.  If we agree its one 2bit state field then I should refactor to enum and switch to clarify.",
      "parentUuid": "a185ac8b_e69f9ac4",
      "revId": "5893c7dd80f0000c3267ae7b1512ac140e7feeb6",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba",
      "unresolved": false
    },
