      "side": 1,
      "message": "There may be a valid case here if irq \u0026 lvl \u0026 !cur_lvl i.e. you get a message setting the HPD high and indicting an interrupt. 3.15.2.1.2 contemplates this happening: If a single message represents both a transition to HPD_High and an IRQ_HPD, the converter\nshall ensure that HPD is taken high for a minimum of 2ms before generating the IRQ_HPD",
      "revId": "5893c7dd80f0000c3267ae7b1512ac140e7feeb6",
